<title>LITHUANIA: LITHUANIA - YIELDS ON 91-DAY T-BILLS FALL.</title>
<headline>LITHUANIA - YIELDS ON 91-DAY T-BILLS FALL.</headline>
<dateline>VILNIUS 1997-04-07</dateline>
<text>
<p>Yields fell on 91-day</p>
<p>Lithuanian Treasury bills on Monday and all of the 50 million</p>
<p>litas issue was sold as it was oversubscribed, the country's</p>
<p>central bank said.</p>
<p>The average yield was 11.05 percent, down from the 11.25</p>
<p>percent offered to buyers at the last auction for 91-day paper</p>
<p>on March 25.</p>
<p>The settlement date is April 10 and the bills mature on</p>
<p>July 10.</p>
<p>All figures aside from yields and days in millions of</p>
<p>litas.</p>
<p>SOLD  DAYS MIN/MAX YIELD  AV. YIELD   LAST AV. YIELD  DEMAND</p>
<p>50    91   10.45/11.50	11.05	    11.25	100.739</p>
<p>--Ed Stoddard, Vilnius newsroom +370 2 22 35 18</p>
</text>
